{
  "_id": "6a39b8f54c3da884a928da6a",
  "Package": "TSENAT",
  "Type": "Package",
  "Title": "Tsallis Entropy Analysis Toolbox",
  "Version": "0.99.24",
  "Authors@R": "person(given = \"Crist\u00f3bal\", family = \"Gallardo\", role = c(\"aut\", \"cre\"), email = \"gallardoalba@pm.me\", comment=c(ORCID=\"0000-0002-5752-2155\"))",
  "Description": "Quantifies and models isoform-usage complexity in RNA-seq\ndata using Tsallis entropy, a scale-dependent diversity\nmeasure. By tuning the entropic index parameter (q), TSENAT\nexamines transcriptome heterogeneity at different scales: rare\nvariants (low q) or dominant isoforms (high q). It enables\ncomputing Tsallis entropy and Tsallis divergence from\ntranscript-level estimates, comparing measures between\nconditions, testing for differences, and visualizing\nscale-dependent complexity via q-curves.",
